  "behavior": [
    "Lease list/add/renew/release use the bounded prepared client and shared durable writer; no foreground fallback.",
    "Legacy explicit TTL authority remains. This checkpoint introduces no workspace expiry default or lifetime conversion.",
    "List reads complete bounded index metadata and retained pages without target or quarantine probes and without the legacy lock.",
    "Native directory, stable-lock, marker and index units retain intent before effect. Marker/index edits hold the unchanged legacy lock; a busy lock refuses promptly.",
    "Add publishes marker before index. Release publishes index before matching marker removal and never removes the workspace.",
    "Only durably observed, exact owned state-directory publications may advance the original prepared missing namespace prefix. Caller, home, config and remaining inputs stay bound.",
    "Unknown index schemas, markers, roles and replacements refuse affected writes. A copied recognized marker requires fresh explicit add intent.",
    "Uncertain effects retain exclusion after worker exit and writer reopen; original receipt replay never repeats a unit.",
    "Lease actor attribution uses explicit actor, explicit owner, then explicit REAP_OWNER. The fallback owner label does not identify a creator.",
    "Renew and release resolution do not read .reap. A final preservation veto can retain a marker after index release; that outcome is partial, not completed success.",
    "Edited integration harnesses require terminal lease completion and preserve unconfirmed fixtures. Fixture Git commits retain configured authorship and disable hooks."
  ],
